# GNSS proposal for Blastoise (ArduRover 4.6.3, CubeOrange+, Here4 rover on DroneCAN node 124), 2026-10-25.
# PROPOSAL ONLY: the owner writes these, on land and disarmed, then reboots and snapshots into this
# directory (README "FCU parameters"). Diff against blastoise.param first. Each line is NAME,value.
#
# Rate: 10 Hz with RTK, not 20 Hz.
# - ArduPilot 4.6 allows GPS1_RATE_MS 50..200, but a DroneCAN GPS ignores the FCU's value
#   (AP_GPS_DroneCAN never reads it, Rover-4.6.3). The rate is the Here4 node's own GPS1_RATE_MS
#   (CubePilot GNSSPeriph Parameters.cpp; older node firmware calls it GPS_RATE_MS).
# - u-blox F9P maximum RTK rate (ZED-F9P datasheet): 4 GNSS 8 Hz, 3 GNSS 10 Hz, 2 GNSS 15 Hz,
#   GPS only 20 Hz. The Here4 manual's "up to 20 Hz" is GPS only, which halves the satellites and
#   makes fixes slower and less robust (the 10-24/25 tests already struggled for a fix).
# - So 10 Hz with GPS+GLONASS+Galileo (BeiDou off) is the highest rate that keeps multi-GNSS RTK.
#   MAVROS asks GPS_RAW_INT at 10 Hz to match (config/mavros_setup.yaml '24:10').
#
# Here4 node 124 parameters: set these in Mission Planner > Setup > Optional Hardware > DroneCAN,
# node 124 > Parameters (not in this FCU file), then reboot the node:
#   GPS1_RATE_MS   100   (was 200)   10 Hz
#   GPS1_GNSS_MODE 69    (was 0)     GPS 1 + Galileo 4 + GLONASS 64; BeiDou off for the 10 Hz RTK limit
#   GPS_AUTO_CONFIG 1    (keep)      the node writes rate and GNSS to the F9P at boot
# Back out: node GPS1_RATE_MS 200, GPS1_GNSS_MODE 0, and '24:5' in mavros_setup.yaml.
#
# FCU parameters:
# Ignored for DroneCAN; kept equal to the node's rate so a reader is not misled.
GPS1_RATE_MS,100
# Measurement lag the EKF compensates. 0 = the driver's default, which for a DroneCAN GPS is the
# generic 200 ms (GPS_Backend.h); the serial u-blox driver uses 120 ms for an F9 (AP_GPS_UBLOX.cpp).
GPS1_DELAY_MS,120
# Lever arms (GPS1_POS_*, INS_POS1..3_*) are not pinned here: the URDF is their one source. Print
# them with `python3 -m mhseals_nav.robot_geometry` (FRD metres from base_link, gps_link and imu_link
# of description/blastoise/blastoise.xacro with y and z negated; test_fcu_lever_arms checks them).
# The IMU offset makes base_link the body origin, so GPS1_POS_* are from base_link too.
# Unchanged on purpose: GPS_INJECT_TO 127 (corrections reach the Here4), GPS1_TYPE 9, GPS_AUTO_CONFIG 1.
